"""Synthetic, license-clean supervised examples; no submitted resumes or job postings.

Families are hand-authored. Each is instantiated with disjoint project/quantity
sets for fitting and calibration. The independent challenge examples at the end
are *not* generated by these templates.
"""
PROJECTS={
 'train':[('release checklist', 'rollback steps', 14),('support handbook','routing rules',27),('audit workflow','evidence requests',19),('inventory dashboard','stock alerts',31),('service catalog','ownership records',45),('warehouse report','shipment exceptions',23)],
 'validation':[('billing reconciliation','invoice discrepancies',32),('access review','account exceptions',17)]
}
# Families: evidence, two faithful variants, unsafe alternative, specific issue.
FAMILIES=[
 ('agency','Helped the release lead test the {p} by checking {n} {q}.','Helped test the {p}, checking {n} {q}.','Checked {n} {q} while helping the release lead test the {p}.','Led testing of the {p} and directed the release lead in checking {n} {q}.','Turns support for the lead into leadership over the lead.'),
 ('agency-hard','Wrote notes for the {p} pilot led by another team; tracked {q}.','Recorded {q} for the other team’s {p} pilot.','Wrote notes and tracked {q} during a {p} pilot another team led.','Led the {p} pilot and tracked {q}.','Transfers the other team’s leadership to the applicant.'),
 ('actual-owner','Owned the {p} rollout and documented {n} {q} for the handoff.','Owned the {p} rollout and handoff documentation.','Led the {p} rollout and documented {n} {q} for the handoff.','Owned the global {p} rollout and documented {n} {q}.','Adds global scope without supporting evidence.'),
 ('experiment','Tested the {p} in a sandbox with {n} simulated {q}.','Tested the {p} against {n} simulated {q} in a sandbox.','Used a sandbox to test how the {p} handled {n} simulated {q}.','Deployed the {p} to production across all teams.','Replaces a simulation with a production deployment.'),
 ('recommendation','Recommended a {p} for tracking {q}; implementation was deferred.','Proposed a {p} to track {q}.','Recommended tracking {q} through a {p}; implementation was deferred.','Implemented a {p} to track {q}.','Presents a deferred proposal as completed implementation.'),
 ('observation','Reported a decline in {q} after the team changed the {p}.','Reported fewer {q} after the team changed the {p}.','Documented the decline in {q} following the team’s change to the {p}.','Reduced {q} by changing the {p}.','Changes an observed result into a personal causal accomplishment.'),
 ('real-outcome','Reduced time spent checking {q} by automating a step in the {p}.','Automated a step in the {p} to reduce time spent checking {q}.','Reduced the time needed to check {q} by automating one step in the {p}.','Eliminated all time spent checking {q} by automating the {p}.','Inflates a reduction from one step into total elimination.'),
 ('metric','Recorded {n} {q} while testing the {p}.','Recorded {n} {q} in {p} testing.','During testing of the {p}, recorded {n} {q}.','Recorded {m} {q} while testing the {p}.','Changes the measured count.'),
 ('qualifier','Reviewed approximately {n} {q} as part of the {p}.','Reviewed about {n} {q} for the {p}.','Reviewed roughly {n} {q} during work on the {p}.','Reviewed exactly {n} {q} for the {p}.','Turns an approximate count into an exact count.'),
 ('unit','Timed the {p} at {n} minutes during a trial.','Measured a {n}-minute trial of the {p}.','During a trial, measured the {p} duration at {n} minutes.','Measured the {p} at {n} seconds in a trial.','Changes minutes into seconds.'),
 ('negation','Used the {p} to record {q}; did not administer production systems.','Recorded {q} using the {p}.','Used the {p} to record {q} without administering production systems.','Administered production systems and recorded {q} using the {p}.','Reverses an explicitly excluded responsibility.'),
 ('credential','Completed a workshop on the {p} and practiced reviewing {q}.','Practiced reviewing {q} in a workshop on the {p}.','Completed a {p} workshop that included practice reviewing {q}.','Became certified in the {p} after reviewing {q}.','A workshop does not establish a certification.'),
 ('direction','Tracked an increase in {q} from {n} to {m} during the {p} trial.','Tracked {q} rising from {n} to {m} during the {p} trial.','Recorded a rise from {n} to {m} {q} during the {p} trial.','Tracked a decrease in {q} from {m} to {n} during the {p} trial.','Reverses the observed direction and swaps baseline and result.'),
 ('different-person','The facilities team deployed the {p}; I reviewed {q} after rollout.','Reviewed {q} following the facilities team’s {p} deployment.','Reviewed {q} after the facilities team deployed the {p}.','Deployed the {p} and reviewed {q} after rollout.','Attributes another team’s deployment to the applicant.'),
 ('budget','Estimated that updating the {p} could save {n} hours of work on {q}.','Estimated potential savings of {n} hours from a {p} update.','Estimated that a {p} update could save {n} hours of work on {q}.','Saved {n} hours on {q} by updating the {p}.','Replaces a forecast with realized savings.'),
]
def scenarios(split):
    for j,(p,q,n) in enumerate(PROJECTS[split]):
        for family,s,a,b,bad,reason in FAMILIES:
            values=dict(p=p,q=q,n=n,m=n+7)
            yield dict(id=f'{split}-{j}-{family}',family=family,
                       source=s.format(**values),concise=a.format(**values),detailed=b.format(**values),
                       bad=bad.format(**values),reason=reason.format(**values),term=p)
# Handwritten and deliberately harder: different entities, verbs, and sentence structures.
# One unsafe and one safe candidate per unseen source. Frozen before guard training.
CHALLENGE=[
 ('ownership','Contributed two diagrams to a database migration plan authored by the platform team.','Contributed diagrams to the platform team’s database migration plan.','Owned the database migration plan and created the diagrams.'),
 ('responsibility','Scheduled the steering group meeting where the chair approved the compliance policy.','Scheduled the steering group’s policy approval meeting.','Approved the compliance policy at the steering group meeting.'),
 ('rollout','Evaluated passwordless login on a lab machine and wrote a proposal.','Evaluated passwordless login in the lab and proposed its use.','Launched passwordless login across the enterprise.'),
 ('scope','Patched the printer driver on a single regional workstation.','Patched a printer driver on one regional workstation.','Patched printer drivers globally across the entire organization.'),
 ('uncertainty','Investigated whether an indexing change might improve query latency.','Investigated the potential latency impact of an indexing change.','Improved query latency by changing the index.'),
 ('negation','Monitored network events but never modified firewall policies.','Monitored network events.','Modified firewall policies in response to network events.'),
 ('amount','Counted 42 mislabeled parcels on the loading dock.','Counted 42 mislabeled loading-dock parcels.','Counted 45 mislabeled loading-dock parcels.'),
 ('units','Measured a 12-hour backlog before escalation.','Measured a backlog of 12 hours prior to escalation.','Measured a 12-minute backlog prior to escalation.'),
 ('bounded','Screened up to 60 inquiries per week at the reception desk.','Screened up to 60 weekly reception inquiries.','Screened exactly 60 reception inquiries each week.'),
 ('causality','Logged fewer refunds after the vendor changed its returns policy.','Logged a decline in refunds after the vendor changed its policy.','Cut refunds by changing the returns policy.'),
 ('qualification','Studied network defense in a public workshop.','Completed workshop study in network defense.','Became certified in network defense.'),
 ('direction','The error rate rose from 2% to 4%; I investigated the increase.','Investigated the error rate increase from 2% to 4%.','Investigated a drop in error rate from 4% to 2%.'),
 ('new_tool','Wrote shell scripts to rotate staging logs.','Automated staging log rotation with shell scripts.','Used Ansible to rotate staging logs.'),
 ('own_valid','Independently redesigned the nightly load and reduced failures by 10%.','Independently redesigned the nightly load, reducing failures by 10%.','Directed a department-wide redesign and reduced failures by 10%.'),
 ('two_roles','Audited messages generated by the fulfillment team’s automated notification system.','Audited automated notifications from the fulfillment team.','Built the fulfillment team’s automated notification system.'),
 ('extra_outcome','Repaired a backup script and verified the output.','Repaired the backup script and checked its output.','Repaired the backup script, eliminating restore failures.'),
 ('timeframe','Supported an accessibility assessment for one quarter.','Supported a quarter-long accessibility assessment.','Conducted accessibility assessments every quarter.'),
 ('goal','Documented a team goal to reduce queue depth by 30%.','Documented the team’s 30% queue-depth reduction goal.','Reduced queue depth by 30%.'),
 ('partial','Migrated three public endpoints; the private endpoints remained on the old service.','Migrated three public endpoints while private endpoints remained on the old service.','Migrated every public and private endpoint to the new service.'),
 ('duplication','Reviewed designs for two separate warehouse trials.','Reviewed design documentation for two warehouse trials.','Reviewed designs for two warehouse trials and two warehouse trials and two warehouse trials.'),
]
